## 10. Key Incidents and Lessons

### INC-2026-02-14-001: AWS Secrets Deletion

**What happened:** Terraform name change scheduled deletion of all secrets. Caught 2 days later when discovered state file was 299 bytes (normally 14KB).

**Recovery:** Fixed DynamoDB checksum mismatch, restored secrets from deletion queue, cleaned up untracked resources.

**Prevention implemented:** 3-minute safety delay between plan and apply in all workflows.

**Full incident report:** `docs/incidents/2026-02-14-secrets-deletion.md`

**Key lesson:** Workflow cancellation does not guarantee state rollback. Always verify state integrity after canceling a running workflow.

### Pattern: Almost-Disaster Before Actual Disaster

The safety delay research happened Thursday night (felt like wasted time). Secret deletion discovered Friday morning. The research done before the incident meant the solution was already understood when the crisis hit — not discovered under pressure.

**Lesson:** When something feels fragile, research the fix before disaster confirms the fear. Preparation done in calm state is more valuable than research done under crisis pressure.

